[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-Mending/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-01-overview.png[/img]
[b]Repair damaged apparel and weapons instead of throwing them away.[/b] Build a hand mending station, an electrical mending station, or a fully automated industrial repair center.

A repair has no flat price. Materials, work time, waste and the chance of botching it all scale with how damaged the item is and how skilled the mender is. Every repair produces real waste. That's the core mechanic, not an optional extra.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-Mending/refs/heads/main/Workshop/glance.png[/img]

[b]Required[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url]
[*][b]Biotech[/b]: the repair center is built around a basic subcore
[*][url=[VRE WORKSHOP LINK]]Vanilla Recycling Expanded[/url]: provides the trash that repairs produce
[/list]

